# The model provider credential, and nothing else.
#
# A SEPARATE FILE ON PURPOSE. `ALPHA_ROADMAP.md` section 4's wave 14 row asks for "a
# documented environment that never places a provider credential in the `.env` the
# Makefile allow-lists", and `OWNER_RULINGS_2026-09-17.md` section 3 adds the rest: "No
# secret belongs in a chat message -- the credential goes on that host's disk, by the
# owner", exactly as `LIVE_RUN_INSTRUCTIONS.md` section 2 already says for this repository.
#
# So this file is written on the host, by the owner, and is never committed, never passed
# to `--env-file`, and never read by anything but the `api` container:
#
# WHAT `--env-file` WOULD ACTUALLY COST, MEASURED BY `W26-HOST` RATHER THAN RECALLED --
# because this comment used to claim more than is true. Passing it to `--env-file` would
# put these names into **compose substitution**, where `${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}` could be
# interpolated into an image tag, a container name or a label. Keeping them out of it is
# real and it is why this file exists.
#
# IT IS NOT TRUE, HOWEVER, THAT THE CREDENTIAL STAYS OUT OF `docker compose config`.
# Driven on Docker Compose v5.3.1: with a sentinel in this file and NO `--env-file`
# pointing at it, `docker compose --env-file env/alpha.env -f compose.server.yml config`
# prints
#
#     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: <the sentinel, in clear>
#
# because `config` RESOLVES `env_file:` into `environment:` before rendering. The flag that
# does not is `--no-env-resolution`, which leaves `env_file:` as a reference:
#
#     docker compose --env-file infra/deploy/env/alpha.env \
#       -f infra/deploy/compose.server.yml config --no-env-resolution
#
# TREAT `docker compose config` OUTPUT AS A SECRET. It also prints every value from
# `alpha.env`, including `AUDITMANAGER_API_TOKEN` and both passwords -- that was always
# true and is worth saying once. It is never pasted anywhere, per the credential rule in
# `OWNER_RULINGS_2026-09-17.md` section 3.
#
# By contrast the TLS private key really is invisible to it: `proxy/compose.tls.yml`
# reaches it through a read-only BIND MOUNT, so what `config` prints is the path
# `/.../infra/deploy/proxy/tls` and never a byte of the file. Measured the same way, with a
# sentinel key in place: `docs/program/reviews/W26-HOST.md` section 3.

#
#   cp infra/deploy/env/provider.env.example infra/deploy/env/provider.env
#   chmod 600 infra/deploy/env/provider.env
#   # then edit it in place on the host
#
# With `AUDITMANAGER_PROVIDER_MODE=recorded` -- the default in alpha.env.example -- none of
# these is read and the file may stay as it is. `settings.load` refuses to start in `live`
# mode without ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and in `proxy` mode without both PROXY_LLM_ names, which
# is the point: a process that cannot make the call it was configured for does not start.

# --- mode `live`: Anthropic's own API ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- mode `proxy`: the model proxy. `OD-02` was revised to the proxy on 2026-09-14. ---
PROXY_LLM_BASE_URL=
PROXY_LLM_TOKEN=
# The stub that means "I am not choosing a model", so the operator's default and its
# fallback chain apply. Any other value is a real choice that changes routing and billing.
PROXY_LLM_MODEL=proxy

# --- optional, both modes ---
# Defaults to the `OD-03` ceiling of USD 1.00 when unset. A run over the eight-page corpus
# costs roughly $0.20 at the recorded rates.
AUDITMANAGER_RUN_COST_CEILING_USD=
AUDITMANAGER_MODEL_ID=
